module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.one_type_variable_bound_to_two_distinct_coproducts

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data one_type_variable_bound_to_two_distinct_coproducts: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "one_type_variable_bound_to_two_distinct_coproducts" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: one type variable is bound by two actuals of distinct types (variants of two different coproducts, or Int and Bool) and the program is Accepted.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: a non-generic f(a: P) called with Q1 is refused (TypeMismatch Coproduct(P) vs Coproduct(Q)). Constructor expressions already elaborate to the owner coproduct. The hole was generic rebind, not variant-to-coproduct typing.",

    "HARM: silent wrongness (DESIGN section 5 / section 4b values inhabit declared types). Two inhabitants of unrelated coproducts share one type variable.",

    "AUTHORED ON THE V1 .dag AND NOW EXECUTED ON THE SEED (review 80480; superseded at the 2751b200 seed regeneration of #14152). v1.compiler.infer unify_generics returns UnifyGenericsAcc and names a later actual that node_type_equals rejects, and the shipped mirror src/v1/stage0/src/v1_compiler_infer.rs now carries that same fold (its unify_generics returns Rc<UnifyGenericsAcc> and emits the two-leg diagnostic at v1_compiler_infer.rs:24303 onward). The pre-regen state described below was true of fa06f6b45ca and is false of 2751b200.",

    "RUNG HONESTY: EXECUTED RUNG on the source->shipped-seed path is 3 (structurally guaranteed), MEASURED on 2751b200 both sides of the variable. The variable is the seed's execution, not the .dag: the same four reject controls are FALSE against the pre-regen seed (fa06f6b45ca, first-wins) and TRUE against the regenerated one, at accepted positive controls of the identical call shape. Controls live in src/v1/tests/src/cross_coproduct_generic_locate_test.rs (same_arm_two_distinct_coproducts_refuses_with_the_fold_message, same_arm_int_bool_refuses_with_the_fold_message, applied_constructor_same_head_differing_argument_list_refuses) and assert the fold's OWN diagnostic shape -- 'bound as' plus '(first argument)' plus '(later argument)' -- so they cannot go green on a fold that never emits it. Matched on shape rather than on a variable letter because the fold names the generic's own name; a hardcoded 'T' made the Box<Int> vs Box<Bool> row read green on both seeds while the fold was in fact refusing it under the name A. THE CLASS IS NOT TOP-RUNG: on the source->v1 Rust emission path there is no reject case and no gate, which is the declared drop below, and a class's rung is the MINIMUM across its in-scope paths (DESIGN section 6b meta-obligation 1). CEILING: 3 on the seed path; the emitted path must reach it before rung 4 or the constructor-tag climb's last step. WHAT A TYPE NAME OR A .dag FOLD ESTABLISHES IS NOTHING: the .dag fold has been in the tree since 8f8f92f80c1 and established nothing until the seed carried it and a discriminating RED executed against it.",

    "DECLARED RUNG DROP (DESIGN section 6b meta-obligation 3, so the loss is tracked rather than silent): ON THE source->v1 Rust EMISSION PATH THIS CLASS IS ONE RUNG BELOW THE LADDER, SILENT, because no reject case exists there to run. src/v1/05_emit_rust.dag emits unify_generics by copying v1/stage0/src/v1_compiler_infer.rs and no gate inspects the emitted unify_generics; a first-wins fold reaching the emitted tree would surface nowhere. previous rung 2, temporary rung 1, reason: the seed regeneration regenerated the mirror FROM the fold and added no emitted-tree consumer, and no reject case was ever authored on the emission path. bounded population: one fold, one emission target, one class. RESTORE (the CAPABILITY, not an artifact): the emitted tree carries a reject control over its own emitted unify_generics whose RED goes false against an emitted first-wins fold and whose accept control stays green.",

    "RESIDUAL, NOT THIS CLIMB: ConstructorTag<P> {} == ConstructorTag<Q> {} is still Accepted. That is operator follow-up C, not a green control of this class. NEXT TRIGGER for C: a typecheck refusal of that equality (or a declared reason it is a different class). A SECOND ROUTE, ALSO OPEN AND UNFIXED, IS NAMED SO IT IS NOT MISTAKEN FOR A RUNG: 'type A = B' makes alias A and alias B equal by RHS equality, and alias_rhs_of_decl returns None for a NON-LEAF rhs (src/v1/04_types.dag), so a chain stops there. The two known_red_probe rows on alias_route_probe_red in dag/gunbc/explicit_witness_admission.dag are THAT class and were not discharged here; do not read the discharge below as covering them.",

    "QUARANTINE GONE (dissolved at 2751b200, DESIGN section 6b meta-obligation 4: the RED stays enrolled, the quarantine goes). Both dissolve_on wordings of the two known_red_probe rows on constructor_tag_route_probe_red named two conjuncts, and both now hold on the shipped seed: (a) v1_compiler_infer.rs unify_generics returns UnifyGenericsAcc -- true at 2751b200 (36 occurrences; 0 at fa06f6b45ca); (b) the probe refuses rather than being first-wins Accepted. For (b) the probe source is compiled verbatim by src/v1/tests/src/cross_coproduct_probe_discharge_test.rs::probe_one_t_two_coproducts_compiles_to_a_refusal, which requires the refusal to BE the rebind refusal rather than any blocking diagnostic, with probe_same_tag_side_by_side_is_still_accepted as its positive control. WHY THE ROWS LEAVE AND THE TEST STAYS: a runtime bool claim cannot discharge a compile-time exit condition -- the witness returned false at both heads, because a compile refusal at the call makes the whole module fail to compile and the claim never reaches a verdict; and cadence QuarantineProbeExpectRed has no executing consumer in this tree (the falsifier.yml runner that consumed it was deleted in 611fd02770), so a row left in that cadence is a ledger entry nothing runs. The former dag/test/claim/constructor_tag_route_probe_red.dag and its src/v2/test/claim/manual copy are deleted; both carried the same body, the same witness, and the same exit condition, so one of them was already a duplicate. Accept controls stay in test.claim.cross_coproduct_generic_locate. Defect cases are still not merge-checked as blocking_count == 0.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "unify_generics", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.cross_coproduct_generic_locate", decl_name: "same_arm_same_coproduct_is_accepted", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.cross_coproduct_generic_locate", decl_name: "same_arm_int_int_is_accepted", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.cross_coproduct_generic_locate", decl_name: "same_arm_two_applied_box_int_is_accepted", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.cross_coproduct_generic_locate", decl_name: "same_arm_two_distinct_coproduct_values_refuse", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.cross_coproduct_generic_locate", decl_name: "same_arm_int_bool_values_refuse", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.cross_coproduct_generic_locate", decl_name: "same_arm_nested_two_distinct_coproduct_values_refuse", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
